# CoW 2G — mutation in a nested for's ELSE body inside a loop. `cow_after_stmt`'s
# For arm destructured only `body`, dropping `else_body` (unlike the While arm),
# so a mutation in `for … else: xs.pop()` was prescan-blind. With the 2G
# For-else scan the outer while's pre-header materialize catches it.
#
# In known_gaps/ (out of the runtime-diff corpus) pending the self-host CoW-2G
# mirror. Rust lane is correct.
void f(Vector[int] xs):
    int n = 0
    while n < 2:
        for i in 0..0:
            print(i)
        else:
            xs.pop()
        n = n + 1
    print(xs.len())

void main():
    Vector[int] a = [1, 2, 3, 4]
    f(a)
    print(a.len())
